@format 1
@id media-loading.in-global-interface
@title In Global interface
@section Media loading
@area In Global interface
@entry unload-current, unload-all, startup-restore, relay-source
@summary Show global operations that clear workspace media or directly request a viewer source.
@related media-loading.common.workspace-media-clear, media-loading.common.viewer-gate, media-loading.common.media-publication
@tag media
@tag loading
@tag global

@alias window = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainWindow.PWindow
@alias workspace = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.PWorkspace
@alias strip = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.PStrip

[unload-current] Selected-workspace Unload command <input>
- Dispatch Unload to the selected workspace; PWorkspaceMediaClear performs viewer close, flow clear, Files clear, and group clear in that order @ window.PShortcutMediaClose(...)
  @ workspace.PWorkspaceMediaClear(...)
> map:media-loading.common.workspace-media-clear

[unload-all] Unload All command <input>
- Dispatch Unload All; PStripContentClear calls PWorkspaceMediaClear sequentially for every tab workspace @ window.PShortcutRun(...)
  @ strip.PStripContentClear(...)
> map:media-loading.common.workspace-media-clear

[startup-restore] Automatic startup restore <input>
- Require automatic restore, nonblank saved path, and existing file, then queue a Loaded-priority dispatcher callback that calls PViewerSourceOpen on whatever viewer is active when the callback executes @ window.PWindowMediaRestore(...)
> startup-result

[relay-source] Relay source arrival <input>
- Create and select the relay tab, then apply its relay payload to the selected workspace @ window.PWindowRelayAccept(...)
  @ workspace.PWorkspaceRelayApply(...)
> relay-result

[startup-result] Startup restore outcome <decision>
- Continue only when the preconditions caused the viewer-open callback to be queued and an active viewer exists when it executes @ window.PWindowMediaRestore(...)
? "PViewerSourceOpen called" > map:media-loading.common.viewer-gate
? "No restorable/active viewer source" > startup-stop

[relay-result] Relay source outcome <decision>
- PWorkspaceRelayApply requires a viewer and nonblank relay source; before calling PViewerSourceOpen it installs a one-shot PViewerMediaChange handler for later section restoration @ workspace.PWorkspaceRelayApply(...)
? "Viewer call issued" > map:media-loading.common.viewer-gate
? "No viewer or blank relay source" > relay-stop

[startup-stop] Startup restore skipped <output>
= No shared viewer request is made.

[relay-stop] Relay has no media request <output>
= No temporary relay media handler is installed and PViewerSourceOpen is not called.
! Once the one-shot relay handler has been installed, a later PViewerSourceOpen rejection that raises no media event can leave that handler attached until some later viewer-media event occurs; this map reflects the code without treating that as a successful load.
